<title>FRANCE: ADP import traffic up 7.1 pct in September.</title>
<headline>ADP import traffic up 7.1 pct in September.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>September 1996 import traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 45,169 tonnes, an increase of 7.1 percent on the same month last year, Aeroports de Paris,(ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Traffic from North America, the principal region of origin for ADP imports, rose by 5.8 percent on September 1995 to 15,517 tonnes while shipments from the Far East increased by 9.6 percent to 11,221 tonnes.</p>
<p>Shipments to CDG and Orly from the European Union rose by 32.6 percent to 6,066 tonnes while imports from sub-Saharan Africa grew by 26.3 percent to 4,014 tonnes.</p>
<p>In contrast, last month's import traffic from the Middle East fell 15.4 percent to 1,879 tonnes.</p>
<p>Global ADP import traffic in tonnes for September 1996, by region, with percentage change on September 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>     Domestic		  2,484    down   17.7</p>
<p>     European Union	  6,066	up   32.6</p>
<p>     Non-EU Europe	     924    down   12.1</p>
<p>     North Africa		566    down   12.1</p>
<p>     Sub-Saharan Africa    4,014	up   26.3</p>
<p>     North America	  15,517	up    5.5</p>
<p>     French territories    1,022	up    0.5</p>
<p>     Latin America	   1,476    down    5.0</p>
<p>     Middle East	     1,879    down   15.4</p>
<p>     Far East		 11,221	up    9.6</p>
<p>     Total		    45,169	up    7.1</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
